{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And it was in the fortieth year.</b> The verse explains to you that He spoke to them across the Jordan in the fortieth year; that He spoke to them at first in the wilderness of Sinai, in the eleventh month, on the first of the month — that is, thirty-six days before his death." "<b>According to all that HaShem commanded him.</b> And not another prophet."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The reading לך הכתוב (\"the verse explains to you\") is taken at face value; the comment appears to draw a chronological connection between the eleventh-month date and the thirty-six days before Moses' death."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:13.310960591Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}